1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:01,800
There’s a party tonight.

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:04,720
I want to introduce you to someone.

3
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,560
You can bring your friend along.

4
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:07,360
Don’t come.

5
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:07,800
Why not?

6
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:08,880
Didn’t you hear him?

7
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:12,440
If you f*cking come,
I’ll hate you for the rest of my life.

8
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:16,720
Moth, will you paint again?

9
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:19,400
Give me a chance to see your work again.

10
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:21,520
I’m sorry I crossed the line.

11
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:23,280
Is there anything I can help you with?

12
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:24,920
Can I sleep on your lap?

13
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,960
(There are times when
we come up with excuses)

14
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:05,040
(to avoid doing what we should do.)

15
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:12,320
(But eventually,
we have to find the courage to start doing it.)

16
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:28,760
[OISHI NEKO]

17
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:36,920
[SO I CAN JUST ASK ANYTHING?]

18
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:38,440
[SURE.]

19
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:46,400
[WHAT IF I’VE NEVER BEEN
THE COMMITMENT TYPE,]

20
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:48,880
[BUT ONE DAY I ASK SOMEONE
TO BE WITH ME?]

21
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:49,880
[YOU THINK IT COULD WORK?]

22
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:52,480
[DO YOU LIKE THEM A LOT?]

23
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:04,200
[WELL… YEAH.]

24
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:07,520
[THEN TELL THEM.
DON’T OVERTHINK IT.]

25
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:20,440
(But sometimes…)

26
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:25,280
(It’s harder than we thought.)

27
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:32,079
Will you paint again?

28
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:34,120
I am painting.

29
00:03:34,560 --> 00:03:37,840
I’m not talking about those comic characters.

30
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:51,360
Paint again, Moth.

31
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:54,480
Give me a chance to see your work again.

32
00:03:56,280 --> 00:03:58,640
Why don’t we try… getting together?

33
00:04:10,440 --> 00:04:11,360
What should I do?

34
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:13,720
(About what?)

35
00:04:14,720 --> 00:04:16,680
(About art or Dean?)

36
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:18,720
About work.

37
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:21,320
I haven’t asked you anything about Dean yet.

38
00:04:21,959 --> 00:04:26,840
I was just telling you
he asked me to be with him.

39
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:28,320
So what are you going to do?

40
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:29,200
Are you going to be with him?

41
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:29,920
Pun!

42
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:33,000
I’m asking for your advice about my painting.

43
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:34,680
(You’re still not done with that?)

44
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:38,280
(I told you. Just paint whatever you want.)

45
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:40,600
(Follow your heart.)

46
00:04:48,360 --> 00:04:48,920
Well…

47
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:53,320
I’m afraid it won’t turn out right.

48
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:55,880
(Are you talking about the art…)

49
00:04:55,880 --> 00:04:58,640
or your relationship with Dean?

50
00:04:58,760 --> 00:05:00,200
Dean has never been the topic here.

51
00:05:00,440 --> 00:05:02,240
Hey, listen to me.

52
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:05,880
Whatever it is,
overthinking isn’t going to help.

53
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:09,480
What you should do is give it a try.

54
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:11,760
(Then you’ll know
what works and what doesn’t.)

55
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:16,480
(Worrying about it is
only going to keep you stuck.)

56
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:19,880
Are you free tonight?

57
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:21,560
I need a drink.

58
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:23,960
I have plans with Ten.

59
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:30,400
So you’re finally
getting serious with Ten, huh?

60
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:33,200
I’ve been serious from the start.

61
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:35,680
And I’m happy.

62
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:39,360
Do you have a problem with that?

63
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:42,680
No.

64
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:46,800
Whatever it is, just tell me straight.

65
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:57,200
If I tell you, will you promise not to get mad?

66
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:01,680
If I got mad at you that easily, do you think

67
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:05,520
we’d have stayed friends this long?

68
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:06,720
(Say it.)

69
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:18,400
Don’t you think
it’s too soon to get serious with Ten?

70
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:22,840
(In my opinion, Ten doesn’t have any flaws,)

71
00:06:23,440 --> 00:06:27,880
but you’re pretty top-tier yourself.

72
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:31,400
If you’d waited a little longer,

73
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:33,880
(you might’ve found yourself
an even better boyfriend.)

74
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:40,080
Okay.

75
00:06:41,720 --> 00:06:46,200
I might’ve crossed a line. I’m sorry.

76
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:50,880
I get what you’re saying, Moth.

77
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:53,760
But if I want to know

78
00:06:54,159 --> 00:06:56,960
whether Ten is good enough for me,

79
00:06:57,640 --> 00:06:59,440
I have to date him first.

80
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:01,600
Then I’ll know if he’s right for me.

81
00:07:09,360 --> 00:07:14,080
Ten and I might need some time
to get to know each other better.

82
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:19,120
But right now, he makes me happy.

83
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:22,680
Isn’t that enough?

84
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:30,520
Yeah.

85
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:33,640
Then go be with Ten.

86
00:07:34,520 --> 00:07:35,440
I’ll leave you alone now.

87
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:01,800
[WHAT ARE YOU DOING?]

88
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:05,520
[LET’S GO GRAB A DRINK.]

89
00:08:10,320 --> 00:08:11,440
[THIS GUY IS FREAKING LUCKY
TO HAVE SOMEONE LIKE DR. PUN.]

90
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:12,600
[I’LL BE HONEST. I DON’T THINK
THEY’RE A GOOD MATCH.]

91
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:13,720
[YOU SHOULDN’T MEDDLE IN
OTHER PEOPLE’S BUSINESS.]

92
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:14,920
[CARE TO ELABORATE
ON “GOOD MATCH”?]

93
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:24,920
[I’LL BE HONEST. I DON’T THINK
THEY’RE A GOOD MATCH.]

94
00:08:25,680 --> 00:08:26,440
[DELETE.]

95
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:36,440
I’m sorry.

96
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:43,840
Why is your hair such a mess?

97
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:47,840
Traffic was terrible,
so I took a motorbike taxi.

98
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:48,640
Gosh.

99
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:49,880
Are you tired?

100
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:52,960
I can come to you next time.

101
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:53,920
That’s okay.

102
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:55,840
It’s easier for me to come to you.

103
00:09:00,880 --> 00:09:03,880
So where are we eating today?

104
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:08,560
I found a rooftop restaurant.

105
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:13,120
Hey. It looks kind of romantic.

106
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:14,640
Let’s go there.

107
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:29,760
I got caught up with work and skipped lunch.

108
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:33,360
Hungry.

109
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:34,800
I believe you.

110
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:38,720
I’m sorry, Pun.

111
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:40,960
Instead of taking you to a fancy restaurant,

112
00:09:41,520 --> 00:09:42,960
we ended up eating noodles.

113
00:09:45,160 --> 00:09:46,160
It’s all good.

114
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:49,080
Eating together is enough
to make me happy.

115
00:09:50,760 --> 00:09:52,920
Besides, this place makes great food.

116
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:55,440
I have it all the time.

117
00:10:00,440 --> 00:10:01,240
Hmm…

118
00:10:01,680 --> 00:10:02,280
Good?

119
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:04,280
It’s really good.

120
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:06,320
See? I told you.

121
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:08,240
Or maybe you’re just hungry?

122
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:09,320
No.

123
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:11,880
It’s because I’m eating with you.

124
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,080
I’m off tomorrow.

125
00:10:22,160 --> 00:10:24,240
Can I come cook for you at your place?

126
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:27,200
I’ll make enough to
keep in the fridge for later.

127
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:33,640
That way, you won’t let yourself
go hungry like this when you’re busy.

128
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:35,560
I can’t tomorrow.

129
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:37,600
There’s an award ceremony tomorrow.

130
00:10:38,080 --> 00:10:40,200
The film I edited won an award.

131
00:10:43,840 --> 00:10:47,040
Wait, you’re a film editor too?

132
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:51,320
I thought you only edited content videos.

133
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:58,000
Actually, editing films is my main job.

134
00:10:59,400 --> 00:11:04,720
I only edit videos for Dean to help him out.

135
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:09,840
What’s the title of the film you edited?

136
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:12,560
You wouldn’t know it.

137
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:15,720
It’s an indie film. Not very well-known.

138
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:16,960
So what?

139
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:20,000
It’s an award-winning film.

140
00:11:21,360 --> 00:11:22,680
Well, yes.

141
00:11:31,520 --> 00:11:34,680
Why didn’t you tell me this was your job?

142
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:42,840
I didn’t think you’d be interested in films.

143
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:47,440
It’s pretty much the opposite of your world.

144
00:11:50,200 --> 00:11:53,720
Anything about my boyfriend,
of course I’d want to know.

145
00:11:56,760 --> 00:12:01,880
Then how about we go
to the event together tomorrow?

146
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:03,880
Sure.

147
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:07,000
Eat up.

148
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:26,840
I haven’t even finished 10% of my painting.

149
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:30,840
But you should eat.

150
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:32,800
Or I’ll feed you myself.

151
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:35,880
Feed me if you dare.

152
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:50,560
Do you want the normal kind of feeding…
or the special kind?

153
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:53,960
I couldn’t take a special feeding
even if I wanted to.

154
00:12:54,720 --> 00:12:56,280
I still have work to finish.

155
00:12:57,560 --> 00:12:59,440
Is this work really that important?

156
00:12:59,440 --> 00:12:59,960
Hm?

157
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:04,880
If you don’t finish it, do you have to
stop calling yourself an artist?

158
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:06,840
Is it really that bad?

159
00:13:11,560 --> 00:13:12,440
I don’t know.

160
00:13:15,040 --> 00:13:16,520
But I want to make it.

161
00:13:19,120 --> 00:13:21,440
You know, when you’re stressed,

162
00:13:23,120 --> 00:13:24,680
you’re not cute at all.

163
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:27,920
Rephrase.

164
00:13:27,920 --> 00:13:29,720
A little less cute than usual.

165
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:33,680
Okay, let’s do this.

166
00:13:34,360 --> 00:13:35,240
Are you free tomorrow?

167
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:38,600
How could I be?

168
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:40,920
I just told you I haven’t finished my work yet.

169
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:44,000
So you’re just going to
sit in front of your canvas?

170
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:46,480
How are you supposed to
come up with ideas doing that?

171
00:13:46,760 --> 00:13:49,160
Let me take you out to find some inspiration.

172
00:13:51,760 --> 00:13:52,200
Yeah?

173
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:54,360
How?

174
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:57,320
What do you want to do?

175
00:13:57,920 --> 00:13:59,640
Diving?

176
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:02,360
Floral design?

177
00:14:03,160 --> 00:14:04,080
Meditation?

178
00:14:04,080 --> 00:14:06,080
A vacation overseas?

179
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:07,840
Let’s go to Europe for a week.

180
00:14:08,320 --> 00:14:11,840
We can see some great art
and maybe you’ll get inspired.

181
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:12,840
Sounds good?

182
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:17,800
This isn’t about finding inspiration.

183
00:14:24,880 --> 00:14:26,880
Then how would you like me to help?

184
00:14:33,840 --> 00:14:35,240
Thank you for trying to help.

185
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:39,200
But I think I need to…

186
00:14:42,800 --> 00:14:44,400
deal with this on my own.

187
00:14:55,000 --> 00:15:00,040
Can I keep my distance from you for a while?

188
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,520
I need to focus on my work.

189
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:15,280
Oh. Great.

190
00:15:17,520 --> 00:15:22,920
Then I hope you finish your work soon.

191
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:42,360
I’ll head home.

192
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:44,800
Huh?

193
00:15:57,520 --> 00:15:59,920
I understand that
you haven’t painted in a long time,

194
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:01,800
so you might be a little rusty.

195
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:03,760
But trust me, Moth.

196
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:06,320
(You’re talented.)

197
00:16:06,720 --> 00:16:09,040
(I’m sure you’ll create a great piece.)

198
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:12,200
I want to believe you, Mes, but right now,

199
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:16,080
everything feels like a dead end.

200
00:16:16,920 --> 00:16:22,880
I’m not trying to pressure you,
but there’s an exhibition next week.

201
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:24,680
(If you can finish the piece in time,)

202
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:28,600
(I might be able to show it to the curator,
in case they’re interested.)

203
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:30,520
Next week?

204
00:16:31,120 --> 00:16:32,480
I don’t want you to miss this opportunity.

205
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:36,080
Trust me. If you can do it,

206
00:16:36,440 --> 00:16:38,400
(you’ll finally be a full-fledged artist.)

207
00:16:38,880 --> 00:16:41,280
(And you won’t have to waste your time
on something that isn’t right for you.)

208
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:47,720
I’ll try.

209
00:16:48,560 --> 00:16:52,760
(I’ll leave you to it now
so you can focus on your piece.)

210
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:54,440
(Talk later.)

211
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:36,080
[TEN, WHERE ARE YOU?]

212
00:17:58,600 --> 00:17:59,160
Pun.

213
00:18:03,680 --> 00:18:04,680
Why are you looking at me like that?

214
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:08,240
Am I overdressed?

215
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:09,480
No.

216
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:12,200
You look very handsome.

217
00:18:28,120 --> 00:18:29,960
Yay!

218
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:31,800
One more.

219
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:34,680
Yeah!

220
00:18:36,640 --> 00:18:37,600
Thank you.

221
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:49,080
How come you never told me
your job was such a big deal?

222
00:18:49,720 --> 00:18:52,040
Come on. That’s an overstatement.

223
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:54,440
It’s just the indie film scene.

224
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:58,200
Besides, I didn’t think
you’d be interested in something like this.

225
00:18:58,560 --> 00:18:59,640
Of course I’m interested.

226
00:19:01,600 --> 00:19:05,400
All this time, you’re always
the one bragging about me.

227
00:19:06,160 --> 00:19:12,800
But I can’t brag about you when I want to
because you never tell me anything.

228
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:31,280
Someone even said before
that your profile didn’t match mine.

229
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,240
But I didn’t care.

230
00:19:37,680 --> 00:19:42,120
As long as you’re sweet and kind.

231
00:19:48,280 --> 00:19:52,160
Gosh, are you just trying to comfort me?

232
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:54,520
No. I’m serious.

233
00:19:56,600 --> 00:19:59,280
Come to think of it, maybe I’m the one

234
00:20:02,640 --> 00:20:04,640
who bagged a top-tier guy.

235
00:20:05,520 --> 00:20:06,600
You’re exaggerating.

236
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:08,520
Not even close.

237
00:20:10,120 --> 00:20:15,880
My boyfriend is super hot and super talented.

238
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:21,640
Let’s take a photo.

239
00:20:27,280 --> 00:20:28,040
This too.

240
00:20:36,280 --> 00:20:36,920
See?

241
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:38,040
Hey!

242
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:39,560
Posted.

243
00:20:40,760 --> 00:20:41,840
You really have to post that?

244
00:20:43,520 --> 00:20:44,560
Can you do that for me too?

245
00:20:45,360 --> 00:20:46,960
I’m shy.

246
00:20:51,600 --> 00:20:53,280
Mr. Dean, we’d really like to know

247
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:54,520
why you’re not here, sir.

248
00:20:54,520 --> 00:20:56,360
We’re so sad.

249
00:20:56,360 --> 00:20:56,720
True.

250
00:20:56,720 --> 00:21:05,160
[WHAT ARE YOU DOING?]

251
00:21:05,160 --> 00:21:12,240
[MOM]

252
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:17,240
Yes, Mom?

253
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:20,400
(Nothing, son. I just missed you, so I called.)

254
00:21:23,560 --> 00:21:25,640
What are you doing?

255
00:21:25,920 --> 00:21:28,640
(I just finished eating. What about you?)

256
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:29,960
(Are you going out?)

257
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:31,880
No, Mom.

258
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:32,640
I’ve been bored lately.

259
00:21:32,640 --> 00:21:33,400
Don’t really feel like going out.

260
00:21:33,880 --> 00:21:35,800
(Are you with Moth?)

261
00:21:41,320 --> 00:21:41,880
No.

262
00:21:42,120 --> 00:21:44,320
(Is work so busy now?)

263
00:21:44,360 --> 00:21:46,240
(Can you find some time to come home?)

264
00:21:46,440 --> 00:21:48,920
(It’s almost your dad’s birthday.)

265
00:21:48,960 --> 00:21:51,240
(Can you come home
so we can celebrate together?)

266
00:21:51,680 --> 00:21:52,920
Why are we celebrating?

267
00:21:53,760 --> 00:21:55,040
We don’t usually celebrate it.

268
00:21:55,400 --> 00:21:56,440
(I don’t know.)

269
00:21:56,800 --> 00:22:00,040
(I just want to do
something special for him this year.)

270
00:22:00,040 --> 00:22:03,160
(And I want you here too,
so the whole family can be together.)

271
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:04,760
(Please come home, dear.)

272
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:26,160
Hey, Dean!

273
00:22:29,520 --> 00:22:31,080
Why didn’t you come in the morning?

274
00:22:31,160 --> 00:22:32,440
Why did you come now?

275
00:22:32,760 --> 00:22:34,960
Driving at night is dangerous.

276
00:22:35,360 --> 00:22:36,560
To avoid traffic.

277
00:22:37,720 --> 00:22:39,840
Didn’t Moth come with you?

278
00:22:40,240 --> 00:22:41,400
No, Mom.

279
00:22:41,840 --> 00:22:42,680
He’s busy.

280
00:22:44,200 --> 00:22:46,160
You didn’t ask him to come, did you?

281
00:22:47,880 --> 00:22:50,760
Even if I did, he wouldn’t be able to.

282
00:22:51,040 --> 00:22:52,400
He’s busy with important work.

283
00:22:52,520 --> 00:22:54,000
How important could it be?

284
00:22:54,400 --> 00:22:55,960
Why didn’t you ask him first?

285
00:22:56,120 --> 00:22:58,280
Maybe he wanted to come with you.

286
00:23:03,640 --> 00:23:05,360
Honey. Honey.

287
00:23:05,720 --> 00:23:06,720
Look.

288
00:23:07,480 --> 00:23:10,960
Dean rushed home
to celebrate your birthday.

289
00:23:11,080 --> 00:23:13,240
He must’ve missed you so much.

290
00:23:16,640 --> 00:23:17,000
Mm.

291
00:23:19,160 --> 00:23:21,480
I’m going upstairs to hit the sack.

292
00:23:21,680 --> 00:23:22,880
Sure. Get some rest.

293
00:23:23,080 --> 00:23:25,080
Come down for breakfast tomorrow.

294
00:23:25,280 --> 00:23:26,080
Yes, Mom.

295
00:23:57,640 --> 00:24:08,560
[I’LL BE AT MY PARENTS’ HOUSE.]

296
00:24:08,720 --> 00:24:16,400
[FOR HOW LONG?
WHEN WILL YOU BE BACK?]

297
00:24:21,360 --> 00:24:25,040
[DRIVE SAFE.]

298
00:24:32,600 --> 00:24:42,240
[ALREADY HERE.]

299
00:24:42,240 --> 00:25:02,600
[CAN I CALL?]

300
00:25:02,640 --> 00:25:13,760
[LET’S NOT FOR NOW.]

301
00:25:58,400 --> 00:26:01,920
[GOOD NIGHT.]
[HOW ARE YOU?]

302
00:26:12,200 --> 00:26:15,760
[GO DOWNSTAIRS
AND GET YOUR DELIVERY.]

303
00:26:19,520 --> 00:26:22,520
[DON’T PAINT TILL YOU FAINT. — DEAN]

304
00:26:26,400 --> 00:26:27,360
Here you go.

305
00:26:31,040 --> 00:26:34,480
[I’M STILL ALIVE.]

306
00:26:43,120 --> 00:26:45,160
[HAVE YOU FINISHED? — DEAN]

307
00:26:49,920 --> 00:26:52,200
[YOUR MUSCLES WILL GET STIFF
FROM SITTING TOO LONG. — DEAN]

308
00:26:55,080 --> 00:26:57,800
[WHEN YOU SELL YOUR PAINTING,
PAY ME BACK FOR THE FOOD. — DEAN]

309
00:27:27,840 --> 00:27:38,200
[I MISS YOU.]

310
00:27:38,240 --> 00:27:43,240
[MISS YOU TOO.]

311
00:27:57,080 --> 00:27:58,520
I think this is good, Moth.

312
00:27:59,160 --> 00:28:02,280
Your technique has become
a lot more refined.

313
00:28:07,560 --> 00:28:09,000
You looked at it for so long.

314
00:28:09,800 --> 00:28:10,800
Is that all you’re going to say?

315
00:28:13,760 --> 00:28:15,400
Feel free to give me honest criticism.

316
00:28:16,280 --> 00:28:17,200
I can take it.

317
00:28:18,400 --> 00:28:19,440
Don’t overthink it.

318
00:28:21,440 --> 00:28:23,200
I don’t think it has any flaws.

319
00:28:24,880 --> 00:28:26,160
It’s just…

320
00:28:29,000 --> 00:28:31,120
I’ve never seen you
paint anything like this before.

321
00:28:32,960 --> 00:28:34,480
You’re much more romantic now.

322
00:28:41,920 --> 00:28:46,680
But I’m really glad
you’re taking painting seriously again.

323
00:28:53,120 --> 00:28:54,520
Trust me, Moth.

324
00:28:56,320 --> 00:29:01,600
This piece is going to take you somewhere.

325
00:29:05,280 --> 00:29:06,640
It’s just one painting.

326
00:29:08,360 --> 00:29:11,080
It can’t be that life-changing.

327
00:29:15,520 --> 00:29:19,960
Just getting back to doing what you
should be doing is already changing your life.

328
00:29:30,880 --> 00:29:36,160
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

329
00:29:36,240 --> 00:29:37,320
I’m gonna blow it out now.

330
00:29:39,440 --> 00:29:41,920
Yeah!

331
00:29:41,960 --> 00:29:43,840
Happy birthday, Dad.

332
00:29:43,880 --> 00:29:46,360
I wish you good health and a long life.

333
00:29:46,360 --> 00:29:48,560
Live to be a hundred.

334
00:29:48,560 --> 00:29:50,520
Who actually makes it to a hundred?

335
00:29:52,080 --> 00:29:53,000
Hey, Dean.

336
00:29:53,280 --> 00:29:54,280
What’s the hurry?

337
00:29:54,400 --> 00:29:55,920
Give Dad your birthday wish first.

338
00:29:56,080 --> 00:29:58,120
He’s been getting
birthday wishes since this morning.

339
00:29:58,280 --> 00:30:00,960
But the monks
already blessed him this morning.

340
00:30:01,000 --> 00:30:02,280
It’s different.

341
00:30:02,720 --> 00:30:05,280
Wishes from family are the best.

342
00:30:09,040 --> 00:30:13,880
Well then, I wish Mom and Dad would always
love each other like you did on day one.

343
00:30:14,240 --> 00:30:14,920
Good?

344
00:30:17,320 --> 00:30:20,160
Or… I wish you guys
would look younger every day.

345
00:30:23,280 --> 00:30:25,320
Happy birthday, honey.

346
00:30:29,920 --> 00:30:31,520
Where should we cut it?

347
00:30:31,520 --> 00:30:34,560
- How do we cut the cake?
- What do you think?

348
00:30:34,560 --> 00:30:35,480
I think right there.

349
00:30:35,480 --> 00:30:38,000
Here? But I think right here is better.

350
00:30:39,000 --> 00:30:40,360
Have you finished painting?

351
00:30:41,720 --> 00:30:42,800
Congratulations.

352
00:30:43,680 --> 00:30:46,560
Now you can get back to living a normal life.

353
00:30:46,800 --> 00:30:49,000
Whoa. “Living”?

354
00:30:50,120 --> 00:30:51,000
Isn’t that a bit much?

355
00:30:51,440 --> 00:30:54,440
Well, you don’t have to be cooped up
in your room all day anymore.

356
00:30:55,320 --> 00:30:56,960
You can go see a movie, listen to music,

357
00:30:57,120 --> 00:30:58,280
(and eat good food.)

358
00:30:58,400 --> 00:30:59,800
(Isn’t that what living is?)

359
00:31:00,920 --> 00:31:04,720
That’s your way of living, not mine.

360
00:31:06,800 --> 00:31:08,000
(Are you still in Ratchaburi?)

361
00:31:08,840 --> 00:31:09,280
Mm.

362
00:31:10,240 --> 00:31:11,360
You’re staying quite long.

363
00:31:11,880 --> 00:31:13,360
Didn’t you say you didn’t like staying home?

364
00:31:14,040 --> 00:31:18,040
Mom wanted me to stay until Dad’s birthday.

365
00:31:19,280 --> 00:31:23,600
She wanted all her children home
for his birthday for once.

366
00:31:25,680 --> 00:31:26,840
I didn’t want to say no to her.

367
00:31:26,960 --> 00:31:28,160
Dad just blew out the candle.

368
00:31:28,880 --> 00:31:29,760
That’s good.

369
00:31:31,880 --> 00:31:33,440
You’ve partied with everyone in the world.

370
00:31:34,040 --> 00:31:35,440
It’s time to party
with your family for a change.

371
00:31:43,560 --> 00:31:45,040
You didn’t get into a fight
with your dad, did you?

372
00:31:46,360 --> 00:31:47,080
No.

373
00:31:48,840 --> 00:31:49,960
Why would you ask that?

374
00:31:50,440 --> 00:31:52,120
Just asking.

375
00:31:53,320 --> 00:31:53,960
I don’t know.

376
00:31:55,680 --> 00:31:59,360
You told me you and your dad
didn’t see eye to eye.

377
00:31:59,840 --> 00:32:03,040
We haven’t talked much,
so we haven’t had a chance to fight yet.

378
00:32:06,400 --> 00:32:08,520
We’re both giving each other
the silent treatment.

379
00:32:09,400 --> 00:32:10,880
Probably for the best.

380
00:32:16,680 --> 00:32:17,560
Um…

381
00:32:27,280 --> 00:32:28,280
When are you coming back?

382
00:32:28,720 --> 00:32:29,160
Aw.

383
00:32:30,360 --> 00:32:30,880
Why?

384
00:32:31,240 --> 00:32:32,760
You’re answering a question
with a question now?

385
00:32:32,960 --> 00:32:35,760
You should know what I want to hear.

386
00:32:36,960 --> 00:32:39,520
Come on. Say it loud and clear.

387
00:32:41,720 --> 00:32:42,800
I miss you.

388
00:32:44,760 --> 00:32:46,200
The signal isn’t very good.

389
00:32:46,560 --> 00:32:47,840
Can you say that again?

390
00:32:48,160 --> 00:32:48,960
Enough.

391
00:32:51,160 --> 00:32:52,240
I miss you too.

392
00:32:54,920 --> 00:32:56,080
I miss you so damn much.

393
00:32:56,680 --> 00:33:00,960
I miss you so, so, so, so much more.

394
00:33:01,440 --> 00:33:02,720
Why are we competing?

395
00:33:03,000 --> 00:33:04,000
I’m not competing.

396
00:33:04,600 --> 00:33:06,840
Because if I were, I’d definitely win.

397
00:33:07,960 --> 00:33:12,080
I miss you “sooooooo” much,
with a million o’s.

398
00:33:12,160 --> 00:33:13,160
I don’t believe you.

399
00:33:13,280 --> 00:33:14,800
Say that again.
My heart needs some pampering.

400
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:16,640
You’re just imagining things.

401
00:33:17,200 --> 00:33:19,360
Are you a good boy now,
going to bed so early?

402
00:33:28,160 --> 00:33:29,880
Here. Keep this in your fridge.

403
00:33:31,520 --> 00:33:32,240
Thank you.

404
00:33:32,360 --> 00:33:35,040
Next time, don’t forget to bring Moth too.

405
00:33:35,600 --> 00:33:38,040
That way, you won’t be lonely
when you’re home.

406
00:33:38,120 --> 00:33:39,960
Come on, Mom. I wasn’t lonely at all.

407
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:42,200
Yes, you were.

408
00:33:43,960 --> 00:33:46,360
You’re a grown-up now.

409
00:33:46,560 --> 00:33:52,280
We all need someone
by our side to be happy. Got it?

410
00:33:54,240 --> 00:33:56,520
But if you’re going to bring someone home,

411
00:33:56,520 --> 00:33:59,120
make sure you’re clear about
your relationship status first.

412
00:33:59,320 --> 00:34:01,920
If you’re going to keep this up,
don’t bother bringing anyone home.

413
00:34:02,200 --> 00:34:03,320
I feel bad for Moth.

414
00:34:04,160 --> 00:34:05,360
Duen!

415
00:34:05,560 --> 00:34:07,480
You’re such a buzzkill for your little brother.

416
00:34:08,520 --> 00:34:10,199
You always have to pick a fight.

417
00:34:10,440 --> 00:34:12,000
I’m just telling the truth.

418
00:34:13,400 --> 00:34:14,920
Get home safe, though.

419
00:34:17,360 --> 00:34:22,639
Thanks so much for
coming home for Dad’s birthday.

420
00:34:31,080 --> 00:34:31,600
I’m taking off now, Mom.

421
00:34:31,600 --> 00:34:32,199
Okay.

422
00:34:32,600 --> 00:34:33,199
I’ll see you later.

423
00:34:33,880 --> 00:34:34,480
Bye.

424
00:36:26,760 --> 00:36:28,280
Ahem.

425
00:36:39,200 --> 00:36:40,680
Your painting is very beautiful.

426
00:36:43,480 --> 00:36:44,440
It’s freaking stunning.

427
00:36:50,800 --> 00:36:52,240
Do you really like it,
or are you just trying to flatter me?

428
00:36:52,880 --> 00:36:56,120
Well, I’m not as artistic as everyone here,

429
00:36:58,120 --> 00:36:59,480
but I’m not blind.

430
00:37:01,960 --> 00:37:03,280
I can see how much

431
00:37:05,200 --> 00:37:06,520
dedication and attention

432
00:37:09,040 --> 00:37:13,320
you put into every part of the painting.

433
00:37:20,200 --> 00:37:23,880
That alone is enough
to make me see how beautiful it is.

434
00:37:27,120 --> 00:37:28,760
Who said it was just dedication?

435
00:37:32,120 --> 00:37:33,880
I put my longing into it too.

436
00:37:45,960 --> 00:37:47,280
I missed you so damn much.

437
00:38:12,520 --> 00:38:13,840
Congratulations.

438
00:38:15,280 --> 00:38:16,600
Hey, Mes.

439
00:38:18,800 --> 00:38:24,240
Was it a hassle pulling strings to get my work
into the showcase at the last minute?

440
00:38:24,880 --> 00:38:25,960
Who told you that?

441
00:38:26,360 --> 00:38:27,720
I didn’t pull any strings.

442
00:38:27,880 --> 00:38:31,000
I just sent your painting to the curator,
and they were simply interested.

443
00:38:32,320 --> 00:38:35,840
But if you don’t believe me, look at this.

444
00:38:41,800 --> 00:38:43,920
Someone’s already interested in
buying your painting.

445
00:38:48,840 --> 00:38:50,040
Are you the one buying it?

446
00:38:51,720 --> 00:38:54,080
If you are, I’m not selling.

447
00:38:55,080 --> 00:38:56,400
I’m not.

448
00:38:57,040 --> 00:38:59,240
Other people are interested in your art too.

449
00:39:03,000 --> 00:39:03,920
What about you, Dean?

450
00:39:04,760 --> 00:39:06,840
Are you interested in any of the paintings?

451
00:39:07,360 --> 00:39:08,280
I can give you some recommendations.

452
00:39:10,040 --> 00:39:10,480
Sure.

453
00:39:11,240 --> 00:39:12,480
But let me look around first.

454
00:39:12,640 --> 00:39:14,640
I’m not sure which one I want to buy.

455
00:39:17,200 --> 00:39:18,200
I’m going to use the bathroom.

456
00:39:24,600 --> 00:39:25,400
Congratulations.

457
00:39:26,480 --> 00:39:27,360
Thank you.

458
00:39:37,440 --> 00:39:37,800
Hey.

459
00:39:38,520 --> 00:39:40,080
Are you really buying that piece?

460
00:39:40,280 --> 00:39:41,960
You mean the “Beautiful Chaos” one?

461
00:39:43,120 --> 00:39:44,720
It’s pretty cheap.

462
00:39:44,840 --> 00:39:45,920
I’ll just buy it first.

463
00:39:46,040 --> 00:39:46,800
Maybe I’ll get lucky.

464
00:39:46,920 --> 00:39:48,680
The artist becomes famous someday.

465
00:39:49,200 --> 00:39:51,160
Though I seriously doubt it.

466
00:39:51,440 --> 00:39:52,880
It’ll just be another piece
collecting dust in my collection.

467
00:39:54,680 --> 00:39:55,480
That’s true.

468
00:39:55,600 --> 00:39:57,440
Come on. There are
plenty of other paintings to look at.

469
00:39:57,440 --> 00:39:58,320
Let’s go.

470
00:40:04,480 --> 00:40:05,280
Oh, hey.

471
00:40:05,720 --> 00:40:08,000
When are you planning to
paint your next one?

472
00:40:08,720 --> 00:40:10,480
I can contact the sponsor beforehand.

473
00:40:11,280 --> 00:40:15,320
You know what? Someone wants to
buy a whole collection of your work.

474
00:40:15,760 --> 00:40:17,080
We could strike a deal early.

475
00:40:18,800 --> 00:40:19,920
I don’t know yet.

476
00:40:21,000 --> 00:40:23,720
I have to finish up
my ongoing work for my clients first.

477
00:40:24,640 --> 00:40:26,920
I still have a lot of projects pending.

478
00:40:27,840 --> 00:40:29,360
And I don’t want to
push the deadlines back any further.

479
00:40:31,720 --> 00:40:34,000
I want you to take your future more seriously.

480
00:40:41,040 --> 00:40:42,640
I am taking it seriously.

481
00:40:43,360 --> 00:40:48,080
I mean, you should think about
what truly matters in your life,

482
00:40:50,000 --> 00:40:54,040
not something that distracts you
from the path you should be on.

483
00:40:57,160 --> 00:40:58,880
How much is this piece? I’m buying it.

484
00:40:59,200 --> 00:41:00,160
How much did you sell it for?

485
00:41:00,360 --> 00:41:01,320
I’ll pay double.

486
00:41:02,560 --> 00:41:03,360
What’s gotten into you?

487
00:41:03,600 --> 00:41:06,600
Because I know
how hard you worked on this piece.

488
00:41:08,160 --> 00:41:10,320
This work deserves to be more than just

489
00:41:10,320 --> 00:41:12,200
another meaningless piece
in someone’s collection.

490
00:41:13,720 --> 00:41:17,880
The guy buying it doesn’t even know
how much work you put into it

491
00:41:17,880 --> 00:41:21,640
or how many all-nighters
you pulled to finish it.

492
00:41:21,720 --> 00:41:24,320
It’s already reserved.

493
00:41:24,440 --> 00:41:25,600
Do you have the buyer’s number?

494
00:41:27,760 --> 00:41:28,720
I still want it.

495
00:41:31,080 --> 00:41:32,040
It’s okay.

496
00:41:38,680 --> 00:41:39,680
It really is okay.

497
00:41:41,200 --> 00:41:42,240
It’s just a painting.

498
00:41:43,800 --> 00:41:45,280
It’s not that valuable.

499
00:41:46,800 --> 00:41:47,720
Let’s just sell it.

500
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:51,280
But—

501
00:41:51,280 --> 00:41:52,200
Go wait for me outside.

502
00:42:10,120 --> 00:42:11,400
Thank you so much, Mes,

503
00:42:13,280 --> 00:42:18,640
for pushing me
and believing in me all this time.

504
00:42:21,840 --> 00:42:25,480
But I can’t be
the same person who believed

505
00:42:26,520 --> 00:42:30,880
and painted because of you anymore.

506
00:42:33,880 --> 00:42:35,600
Because I’ve realized that

507
00:42:37,600 --> 00:42:42,320
I should dedicate myself
to what truly matters in my life.

508
00:42:44,440 --> 00:42:45,720
What do you mean, Moth?

509
00:42:47,520 --> 00:42:51,360
Your opportunity
and your worth are right here.

510
00:42:54,440 --> 00:42:56,920
(How would you like me to help?)

511
00:42:58,000 --> 00:42:58,960
(I miss you.)

512
00:42:59,440 --> 00:43:00,520
(I miss you too.)

513
00:43:01,160 --> 00:43:02,600
(I missed you so damn much.)

514
00:43:05,320 --> 00:43:09,560
I think we should go our separate ways, Mes.

515
00:43:15,880 --> 00:43:16,920
Will you excuse me?

516
00:43:30,760 --> 00:43:31,360
Where are we going?

517
00:43:31,840 --> 00:43:32,720
You done with the exhibition?

518
00:44:13,720 --> 00:44:15,320
Save your money for something else.

519
00:44:16,680 --> 00:44:18,040
Why would you buy my painting?

520
00:44:19,000 --> 00:44:20,480
Wouldn’t it be nice if I owned it?

521
00:44:22,880 --> 00:44:28,920
Well, it’s not like it’ll be
the last painting I ever make.

522
00:44:31,000 --> 00:44:32,560
I can always paint another one
when I’m in the mood.

523
00:44:33,880 --> 00:44:35,160
You can buy it then.

524
00:44:57,080 --> 00:44:58,440
Can I stay over at your place tonight?

525
00:45:01,320 --> 00:45:02,520
Let’s make something to eat.

526
00:45:08,520 --> 00:45:10,280
Will you stop being so cute?

527
00:45:12,160 --> 00:45:15,840
If I were so crazy about you
that I lost my mind, what would I do?

528
00:45:54,240 --> 00:45:54,880
Making rice porridge?

529
00:45:55,080 --> 00:45:55,400
Yeah.

530
00:45:58,960 --> 00:45:59,840
You smell good.

531
00:46:00,320 --> 00:46:01,120
Duen’s calling.

532
00:46:01,320 --> 00:46:01,720
Why are you calling—

533
00:46:01,720 --> 00:46:04,000
Dad was admitted to the hospital last night.
He needed emergency surgery.

534
00:46:04,080 --> 00:46:05,320
Dean, you should come home.

535
00:46:05,480 --> 00:46:06,840
If I go, how can I help him?

536
00:46:06,840 --> 00:46:08,920
Or will I just make him feel worse?

537
00:46:09,320 --> 00:46:11,920
Just having you there is good enough.

538
00:46:12,240 --> 00:46:13,640
Do you want me there with you?

539
00:46:13,880 --> 00:46:16,880
Please take care of my little brother, Moth.
